
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;ve set up a small IRC server for the Tom&#8217;s IT Cafe community.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">IRC is a lightweight text-based chat system that has been used on the Internet for decades.<br>It&#8217;s simple, fast, and works on almost any device.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The server is fully encrypted and supports SASL authentication and host cloaking.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Connection details:</p>



<span id="more-8889"></span>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Server</strong>: <code>irc.silentarchitect.org</code><br><strong>Port</strong>: <code>6697</code><br><strong>TLS</strong>: <code>required</code></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Suggested clients:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Android: HexDroid<br>Desktop: WeeChat, Irssi, or Pidgin</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Example (WeeChat):</p>


<div class="wp-block-code">
	<div class="cm-editor">
		<div class="cm-scroller">
			
<pre>
<code><div class="cm-line">/server add silent irc.silentarchitect.org/6697 -tls</div><div class="cm-line">/connect silent</div><div class="cm-line"></div></code></pre>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After connecting, you can register your nickname with NickServ.<br>SASL authentication is available after registration.</p>


<div class="wp-block-code">
	<div class="cm-editor">
		<div class="cm-scroller">
			
<pre>
<code><div class="cm-line">/msg NickServ REGISTER password email@example.com</div><div class="cm-line"></div></code></pre>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Discord</strong> will remain the main chat platform, but this IRC server is available for anyone who prefers a lightweight, self-hosted communication channel.</p>



